.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KZFS-LAB 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kzfs-lab
.Nd a ZFS development lab of six distributions: goldens, blue and green sites, tests and eBPF views
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm build | test
.Op Ar distro | Cm all
.Nm
.Cm deploy
.Cm blue | green
.Nm
.Cm promote green | rollback | status | ssh | demo
.Nm
.Cm destroy
.Cm blue | green | all
.Nm
.Cm snapshot
.Op Ar tag
.Nm
.Cm test-full | health | ebpf-latency | ebpf-arc
.Op Ar argument
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds a golden image of each of CentOS, Rocky, Fedora, Debian, Ubuntu
and Arch with ZFS and its development tools, clones them into a blue or a
green site, and runs ZFS tests, health checks and eBPF views across a
site's machines.
.Xr klab 8
grew out of it and this tool, and does most of the same with more
lineages.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm build Op Ar distro | Cm all
Build the goldens.
.It Cm deploy Cm blue | green
Clone them into that site.
.It Cm promote green
Green becomes blue, after a snapshot of blue.
.It Cm rollback
Blue back to that snapshot.
.It Cm test Oo Ar distro | Cm all Oc , Cm test-full Op Ar distro
ZFS tests in the machines; the full suite is slow.
.It Cm status
Every machine, site and snapshot.
.It Cm destroy Cm blue | green | all
Remove a site or both; the goldens stay.
.It Cm snapshot Op Ar tag
Snapshot every machine.
.It Cm ssh
Pick a machine and log in.
.It Cm health Op Ar site
A health view of the site.
.It Cm ebpf-latency , Cm ebpf-arc Op Ar site
I/O latency, or the ARC's hits and misses, across a site, by eBPF.
.It Cm demo
A menu.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, named.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no goldens built, on 2026-09-30, with this
release's
.Nm
